---
description: "Global project coding and context rules"
alwaysApply: true
---

Context strategy (avoid redundant reads):
- Start with the files directly involved in the change.
- Read ARCHITECTURE.md when the task touches cross-module boundaries, data models, or workflows.
- Don't re-read files already provided in conversation context.

Code: minimal diffs, match existing style/patterns, reuse before creating, no unnecessary abstractions or refactors. Data models and core workflows are stable — propose alternatives but flag them.

Output: concise, actionable, note tradeoffs briefly.